#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""020 stated test changes: contracts/test-impact.md "Fact-level expansion", rows TI-10 to TI-70.
PARENT only, at the checkpoint each row names (tasks.md CP-B, CP-C, CP-D, CP-E).

Each row is (row id, checkpoint, file, old, new, expected count). Rows run in list order on an
in-memory copy; every old string's count is asserted against the text left by the rows before it.
A whole-file row (old == RETIRE) deletes a retired test file and asserts that it exists. Any
mismatch aborts with NOTHING written or deleted.

Run from anywhere (paths resolve from the repo root, three levels above this file; TI_ROOT
overrides it, e.g. for a scratch copy):
    DRYRUN=1 python3 specs/020-admin-workspace/evidence/test-impact-edit.py            # all rows, counts only
    python3 specs/020-admin-workspace/evidence/test-impact-edit.py --cp CP-E          # apply one checkpoint
    python3 specs/020-admin-workspace/evidence/test-impact-edit.py TI-10 TI-11        # apply rows by id
    python3 specs/020-admin-workspace/evidence/test-impact-edit.py --cp CP-D TI-34    # both filters (AND)
Output goes to stdout and, when writing (not DRYRUN), is also teed to
evidence/test-impact-edit-<cp or row ids>.txt; `--tee PATH` sets the file in either mode.

Rows are chained: a later checkpoint's row expects the text an earlier checkpoint left (TI-34
CP-D then CP-E, TI-50 CP-B then CP-E, TI-56 CP-B then CP-E). An unfiltered DRYRUN on the
unchanged tree therefore checks every row against the state the checkpoints will see in order.

Old blocks were sliced from the live test files (whole facts by name, sections by their
"// ──" header) by a generator at T009, so they match by construction; new fact bodies keep every
unchanged line of the old fact and change only what the TI row names.
"""
